# Develop and inspect

**Prerequisites:** [Install](/docs/start/install/).
**You will do:** run, view, browse, and inspect the same module from one checkout.
**Verify:** `rocci inspect FILE` prints components and source-map segments.
**Next:** [Use the playground](/docs/how-to/use-the-playground/) or
[CLI](/docs/reference/cli/).

Commands below use the source-checkout spelling.

## Run the app

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/counter
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/counter --no-window
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/counter --no-live-reload
```

`--no-window` prints a URL; the HTTP origin is the same as the preview webview.
`--no-live-reload` pauses automatic refresh; watch still rebuilds. `--log-handlers`
prints matched routes. `-v` shows compile and wait phases.

## Preview one component

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- view \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci \
  --component Hello --arg name=Ada
```

HTTP declarations are ignored. `--component Hello` and `--component hello` both
work.

## Browse fixtures

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- browse examples/rocci/standalone/styling
```

This is the component gallery.

## Inspect lowering

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- inspect examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- inspect --ast examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- ast examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- render examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci --fragment
```

`inspect` always prints source-map segments. `--ast` adds the S-expression tree.
`render` snapshots `Html.render` (not the playground WASM path).

## Dev panel

In the preview window, open Dev. **Performance**, **Source**, and **Console**
are host tools. Console shows runtime lines and teed Roc stderr, not
`@component` logs. Reduce a failure to one `.rocci` file plus the exact command
before filing an issue.

**Related:** [Diagnostics](/docs/reference/diagnostics/),
[Error boundaries](/docs/concepts/error-boundaries/).
